# INVOL option 1 on a DS5500: initialise the virgin physical volume.
#
# `1 -f` -- "don't re-format disk". The medium is a file with no defects to
# find, and the format is what makes this option cost a run of its own.
#
# `Enter verification option: 1` is "no verification"; 2 and 3 write and re-read
# every block to find media defects, which is a long no-op against a file.
#
# `Select disk:` is asked here too, which C50's table lists under option 7
# alone -- it cost a run. `FINDINGS.md` C277.
expect MD14
expect >
send DI C\r
expect >
send EX INVOL\r
expect Option:
send 1 -f\r
expect q=Quit
send w\r
expect Physical volume name
send dn5500\r
expect verification option
send 1\r
expect average file size
send 5\r
expect volume 1:
send all, dn5500\r
expect pre-recorded badspot
send y\r
expect Anything more to do
send n\r
